[h1]RimMCP[/h1]
[i]Agentic intelligence for the Rim.[/i]

[h2]What is this?[/h2]
RimMCP connects your colony to any AI agent with MCP support. Your agent will be able to see and do almost anything in the game.

[i]For the modern high-impact 10x engineer.[/i]

[h2]What does it let agents do?[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]See.[/b] Pawns, stockpiles, bills, research, threats, the map itself, even your mod list and error log.
[*][b]Do.[/b] Zones, stockpiles, blueprints, mining, bills, work priorities, policies, research.
[*][b]Command.[/b] Draft, move, attack, rescue, tend, equip. Use their right-click orders and abilities (Mod actions supported)
[*][b]Time.[/b] Control speed, pause, run the game.
[*][b]Handle.[/b] Read alerts and letters, accept quests, choose rewards, answer dialogs.
[*][b]Prepare agentically[/b] Pick the scenario, world, landing site, ideoligion and colonists through the game's setup screens.
[*][b]Save.[/b] Save, load, and return to the main menu.
[*][b]Talk.[/b] Tell you what they're doing, or send a letter when something needs your attention.
[/list]

[table]
[tr][th]Access Presets[/th][th]Agents can[/th][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Full control[/b] (default)[/td][td]Do everything, including storyteller, difficulty, saves and new games.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Control[/b][/td][td]Run the colony, including letters and quests, but not change game settings, save, load or set up games.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Administration[/b][/td][td]Read, manage colony settings and run time, but not give direct orders.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Read only[/b][/td][td]Look, but no actions.[/td][/tr]
[/table]

Fine-tune access by switching individual tools on or off in mod settings.

[h2]Things to try[/h2]
[list]
[*]"Anyone worth trying to recruit from the injured raiders?"
[*]"Make a corn field on the rich soil, queue up meals."
[*]"Figure out the most efficient fabric available, order clothes for the colony and set up apparel policies."
[*]"Which mod is throwing red errors and why?"
[*]"Destroy the Mechhive, make no mistakes."
[*]"Reroll colonists until we have a well-rounded colony and two shooters."
[*]"Keep me posted on anything that needs my attention."
[/list]

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]RimWorld 1.6 or 1.7[/b].
[*]An AI client with support for local (stdio) MCP servers. Tested with Codex, Claude Code & OpenCode.
[/list]

[h2]Setup[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Enable RimMCP in your mod list and restart the game.
[*]Go to Options > Mod settings > RimMCP and click [b]Copy MCP config[/b].
[*]Add that config to your client's MCP settings (or paste it to your agent and tell it to configure itself, who has time to edit tomls nowadays).
[*]Turn on RimWorld's [b]Run in background[/b] option so requests work while you're alt-tabbed.
[/olist]

[h2]Frequently asked[/h2]
[b]Mid-save compatible?[/b] Yes. Agent letters stay in your History like any other letter, but nothing in your save needs RimMCP. Feel free to add or remove at will.

[b]Performance?[/b] Near 0 impact when idling. When your agent calls tools, most requests are handled in milliseconds. Token wise, full game control and repeatedly reading pawns can consume a lot of tokens, keep an eye on your usage if you're enabling everything. Since 1.2, reading a pawn costs about a third of what it used to.

[b]What is my agent doing?[/b] A cursor with its name shows where it acts. The RimMCP button on the bottom bar opens the agent log: everything it did, and what it was refused and why.

[b]Multiplayer Mod?[/b] Supported, read-only operations will work, but anything that changes the game or the clock is refused during a Multiplayer session.

[b]Privacy?[/b] If your client uses a cloud model, it may send colony data to that provider. Your colony data could help shape the mind of future LLMs, what could possibly go wrong?

